    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-efficiency matchup for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 72.16 score marks him as our premier start. Facing Pallante, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.17 xERA and a significant platoon edge, allowing him to capitalize on the prime #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (66.56) is a high-conviction play against Lowder; despite a minor platoon disadvantage, his placement in the #2 hole and the pitcher's high xERA make him a core contributor for run production today. In the outfield, **Kyle Tucker** (63.20) and **Sam Antonacci** (61.55) provide the necessary consistency to keep us competitive in the categories where speed is at a premium, with **Sam Antonacci** seeing a nice boost from an aggressive leadoff role.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Jorge Polanco**, who landed just outside the starting nine with a 53.21 score. While his matchup against Bibee showed promise, **Jorge Polanco** ultimately fell short due to a suboptimal #8 spot in the order and lower overall efficiency compared to the dynamic upside offered by **Nasim Nunez** and **Heliot Ramos**. We are keeping a close eye on **Jackson Merrill**, whose 61.00 score is based on a pending lineup assumption; should his status change, we have the flexibility to adjust. Furthermore, users should note the 36% rain risk looming over the matchups involving **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson**, both of whom are facing Detmers. While their raw projections remain serviceable, the weather volatility adds a layer of risk to two of our primary middle-of-the-order threats. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg**, whose unavailability remains a challenge as we navigate the home stretch.",
